# Settings › Remote play › Use this PC from anywhere (docs/REMOTE-DESKTOP.md): Sunshine's ports only through Tailscale
# and this PC itself, loaded again when the PC starts. Off in the image: hearth-home-server-helper enables it only when
# the owner turns the feature on, and disables it when he turns it off. It never holds up the boot or a session: it
# isn't ordered before anything, can't fail the boot ("-"), and has a short time limit. Sunshine's own drop-in waits
# for its mark (/run/hearth/remote-desktop-fw): no rule, no Sunshine.
[Unit]
Description=Hearth: Sunshine only through Tailscale (Use this PC from anywhere)
ConditionPathExists=/etc/hearth/remote-desktop.nft
After=local-fs.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
RemainAfterExit=yes
TimeoutStartSec=30
ExecStart=-/usr/bin/python3 /usr/libexec/nimbus/hearth-home-server-helper remote-fw load

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
